//! Unit TR-A acceptance (calc doc §11.1 row TR-A, §9.4 L4): CalcTriggers.lua 1-901 (helpers,
//! `calcMultiSpellRotationImpact`, `helmetFocusHandler`, `CWCHandler`, `defaultTriggerHandler`)
//! against PoB on `triggers:in` → `triggers:out`, with the GlobalCache injected.
//!
//! * Corpus: `corpus/TR-A/*.xml`, one build per case of PoB's own trigger spec
//!   (`spec/System/TestTriggers_spec.lua`: CoC, CWC, Mjölner, Cospri's, Focus, CwDT, the unique
//!   triggers, …), generated by `tra_generate_corpus` (ignored; it runs each spec body in PoB and
//!   saves the build with `build:SaveDB`), plus the `.parity/builds` that contain a trigger.
//! * Dumps: every `triggers:in#n` / `triggers:out#n` hit of every env (the main env and the
//!   recursive `buildActiveSkill` envs), probed by this test into the shared, content-keyed
//!   probe cache (`testkit::probe_selection`; CK1, CCR-0146 §4) when absent (LuaJIT, the
//!   machine-wide oracle lock).
//! * GlobalCache: `findTriggerSkill` / the Manaforged branch call `calcs.buildActiveSkill` (unit
//!   CA, not ported) for a uuid missing from the cache. The test injects `triggers:in`, then adds
//!   the entries of `triggers:out`'s cache whose uuid is absent at `:in` (the ones the call built),
//!   so the Rust run reads exactly what PoB read.
//! * Dispatcher: `calcs.triggers` and `configTable` are TR-B's (not ported yet). The test carries
//!   a scaffold copy of `calcs.triggers` (CalcTriggers.lua 1585-1627) and of the configTable arms
//!   the corpus reaches whose bodies are plain table constructors (see `arm`); a hit whose key has
//!   an arm the scaffold does not carry is counted as `untested (TR-B arm)`, not compared.
//!   TR-B replaces the scaffold with the real dispatcher and re-runs this L4 over every arm.
//!
//! Gate: no hit with a mismatch or a Rust error among the compared hits, and at least one
//! compared hit through each handler (default, CWC, Focus).
//!
//! Knobs: `TRA_BUILDS=stem1,stem2`, `TRA_VERBOSE=1` (every mismatch). A missing input skips with
//! a message; with `POB_ORACLE_REQUIRE=1` (or `CI`) it fails instead.
#![cfg(feature = "luajit")]
#![allow(non_snake_case)]

